# Static website media copied to S3 and excluded from the nightly DirectAdmin
# account backup. Read by /usr/local/sbin/sync-site-media.sh.
#
# Install to /etc/da-vhost-listen/site-media.conf (mode 0644, root-owned).
#
# Format: one entry per line, "<account> <path relative to the account home>".
#
#   - Relative paths only. An absolute path is ignored, not resolved.
#   - No trailing slash. These exact strings are written into
#     .backup_exclude_paths, and GNU tar 1.35 does not exclude a directory given
#     with one -- the media would stay in the archive while the size estimate
#     said otherwise.
#   - No "..".
#
# What belongs here is content that is large, changes rarely, and is served from
# the live site: galleries, video directories, document archives. What does not
# belong here is anything whose only copy would then be an S3 object nobody has
# read back -- run --deep-verify before the first exclusion, and note that the
# nightly account backup stops covering these paths the moment they are listed.
#
# Adding a path here does not exclude it. Excluding is a separate, deliberate
# step (--write-exclusions) that refuses to run without a verified receipt.

# teller: 34 GB of the account's 54 GB, which is why it did not fit the staging
# disk. Churn measured 2026-09-08 over a 90-day window.
#   comsatlegacy gallery   17.3 GB, 33,319 files, 0 changed in 90d
#   steveteller gallery    10.5 GB, 10,479 files, 1,801 changed in 90d (active)
#   comsatlegacy videos     3.2 GB, newest file 6 years old
#   comsatlegacy FromJHU    3.5 GB, newest file 5 years old
#   iotsystems videos       3.1 GB, newest file 7.7 years old
teller domains/comsatlegacy.com/public_html/gallery
teller domains/comsatlegacy.com/public_html/videos
teller domains/comsatlegacy.com/public_html/FromJHU
teller domains/steveteller.com/public_html/gallery
teller domains/iotsystems.com/public_html/videos
